The text font of the NimbleZero screens (/usr/share/nz/fonts/nz-8.nzf)
======================================================================

nz-8.nzf is built by scripts/make-nz-font.py from:

- NimbleZero Sans 8 (nimblezero-sans-8.bdf): Latin with its extensions, Greek, Cyrillic
  and some symbols, 8x8.  Converted from Press Start 2P by CodeMan38 (Copyright 2012 The
  Press Start 2P Project Authors, cody@zone38.net) with scripts/convert-ps2p-to-bdf.py.
  SIL Open Font License 1.1, OFL-nimblezero-sans.txt.  "Press Start 2P" is a Reserved
  Font Name of the original, so this modified version has a name of its own.
- NimbleZero key symbols (nimblezero-keys-8.txt): Enter, Tab, Backspace, Esc, Space,
  Shift, Ctrl, Opt, Page up/down, drawn for NimbleZero.  GPL-2.0-only, or at your
  choice the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
- Fusion Pixel Font 8px, monospaced, release 2026.07.20, by TakWolf
  (https://github.com/TakWolf/fusion-pixel-font): Chinese, Japanese and Korean in four
  forms (ja, zh-hans, zh-hant, ko).  SIL Open Font License 1.1, OFL-fusion-pixel.txt.
  It is assembled from other pixel fonts; their licences are in fusion-pixel-sources/.

Which form of the CJK characters is drawn is set in Options > East Asian text
(/data/etc/nz/east-asian-text); a text that contains kana is always drawn in the
Japanese form.

The font file may be used and passed on under the licences above, as part of NimbleZero
or on its own.
